1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,688
This is The Build Guild, a BAND software factory with clear ownership,
complete handoffs, and independent review.

2
00:00:06,688 --> 00:00:08,656
Our produced application is Tablekeeper.

3
00:00:08,656 --> 00:00:14,557
This video shows the separate Local Sol practice run and its deployed
Stage Two snapshot.

4
00:00:15,207 --> 00:00:17,999
The factory configures seven distinct roles.

5
00:00:17,999 --> 00:00:19,860
PM coordinates the work.

6
00:00:19,860 --> 00:00:24,047
Architect and Designer shape the technical plan and experience.

7
00:00:24,047 --> 00:00:26,839
Backend and Frontend implement attributable changes.

8
00:00:26,839 --> 00:00:31,027
QA checks the candidate, while Reviewer independently decides acceptance.

9
00:00:31,027 --> 00:00:34,284
One active writer lease limits conflicting changes.

10
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:39,867
A complete handoff carries requirements, source digests, evidence, and the
next owner.

11
00:00:40,517 --> 00:00:43,725
Here is the actual Tablekeeper Local Sol room.

12
00:00:43,725 --> 00:00:48,537
PM sends the frozen candidate and full review context to Factory Reviewer.

13
00:00:48,537 --> 00:00:52,947
The message includes source hashes, existing failed evidence, and bounded
instructions.

14
00:00:52,947 --> 00:00:54,952
Reviewer acknowledges that specific handoff.

15
00:00:54,952 --> 00:00:58,962
The receipt confirms delivery; it does not accept the product.

16
00:00:58,962 --> 00:01:03,373
We are reading existing room history, without sending a new task.

17
00:01:04,023 --> 00:01:13,351
Independent review rejects this candidate because keyboard focus can fall
back to the page body after booking recovery, including conflict and
uncertain-response cases.

18
00:01:13,351 --> 00:01:17,812
The reviewer records reproducible failures and requests a bounded Frontend
repair.

19
00:01:17,812 --> 00:01:23,084
Passing other checks does not erase this defect or establish Stage Two
acceptance.

20
00:01:23,734 --> 00:01:27,934
Frontend and Designer acknowledge the finding and preserve the failed
evidence.

21
00:01:27,934 --> 00:01:31,370
Frontend waits for PM to authorize a repair lease.

22
00:01:31,370 --> 00:01:36,715
The recorded deployment still uses the rejected snapshot; a later repair
requires fresh review.

23
00:01:37,365 --> 00:01:39,871
Now we open the real deployed website.

24
00:01:39,871 --> 00:01:46,315
The visible demo notice explains that its restaurants are fictional and
that accounts and reservations reset on restart.

25
00:01:46,315 --> 00:01:49,179
This is a demonstration service with ephemeral storage.

26
00:01:49,829 --> 00:01:55,755
We choose Cedar and Coast, a future date, and six guests, then search live
availability.

27
00:01:55,755 --> 00:01:59,311
Individual tables that cannot fit the party are unavailable.

28
00:01:59,311 --> 00:02:04,842
The Family table and the declared Garden and Corner combination can
accommodate six guests.

29
00:02:04,842 --> 00:02:06,817
Available options are clearly distinguished.

30
00:02:07,467 --> 00:02:11,889
Selecting the table pair while signed out produces the actual login gate.

31
00:02:11,889 --> 00:02:15,206
This recording demonstrates public search and that access boundary.

32
00:02:15,206 --> 00:02:19,997
It does not claim to show a completed booking, private lookup, or
cancellation.

33
00:02:20,647 --> 00:02:23,580
We switch to Olive House and two guests.

34
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:29,080
The live results show the restaurant’s Berlin timezone and both single-
table and declared combination options.

35
00:02:29,080 --> 00:02:32,747
The search follows the selected venue, date, and party size.

36
00:02:33,397 --> 00:02:41,790
The deployed source is the commit shown on screen from the separate Local
Sol practice run, rather than Run Six.

37
00:02:41,790 --> 00:02:46,407
Practice included participant-approved scheduling and budget changes, with
an administrative restart.

38
00:02:46,407 --> 00:02:48,505
The keyboard-focus defect remains disclosed.

39
00:02:48,505 --> 00:02:53,541
This demo does not establish final factory acceptance or persistent
reservation storage.

40
00:02:54,191 --> 00:03:00,394
At eleven twenty-three PM Pacific on October fifth, elapsed time was about
three hours fifteen minutes.

41
00:03:00,394 --> 00:03:06,210
The local run had reported about one hundred four million additional
tokens, including cached input.

42
00:03:06,210 --> 00:03:08,148
These are reported usage counters.

43
00:03:08,148 --> 00:03:13,576
Dollar cost and subscription-quota conversion are unavailable, and the run
was still in progress.

44
00:03:14,226 --> 00:03:21,407
The factory lesson is simple: make ownership and communication explicit,
retain failed evidence, and keep acceptance independent.

45
00:03:21,407 --> 00:03:25,209
Explore the produced Tablekeeper demo at the link shown.
